{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/271581-forsaken-character-suggestions","id":271581,"title":"Forsaken Character Suggestions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-03T06:36:45-07:00","id":271581,"title":"Forsaken Character Suggestions","content":"I made one of these over on Requiem and the same applies to this thread. Coming up with a full character can be difficult for veterans who have writer's block, or new players who have a lot of ideas swimming around. So the purpose of this thread is to provide some pre-written character concepts and backgrounds that players can pick up. All they have to do is fill in the Attributes, Skills, Specialties, Merits, and give the character a description. Everything else has been filled out for them.<br /> <br /> Of course nothing says the player can't adjust a few things when they pick the characters. These are just suggestions, after all.<br /> <br /> <br /> Here are 3 characters that I've written up, although I'm still working on 2 more to complete the whole pack, so those will be posted once I've gotten them done.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Allen (Trickster-of-Battle) Minsk</b><br /> <br /> <b>Concept:</b> Mastermind Strategist<br /> <b>Pack:</b> Teen Wolfpack<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Auspice:</b> Elodoth<br /> <b>Tribe:</b> Storm Lords<br /> <b>Age:</b> 17<br /> <br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Prudence<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Lust<br /> <br /> <b>Primary Renown:</b> Honor, Cunning, Wisdom<br /> <br /> <b>Gifts:</b> Evasion, Insight, Warding<br /> <b>Primal Urge:</b> 2<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 11/1<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Bio:</b> If you had known Allen Minsk before his first change, you would certainly have not considered him werewolf material, and certainly not a member of the Storm Lords, on top of that. Allen wasn't the high school athlete super star that most pack alphas tend to come from. Allen was the captain of the chess team, ranting against fan boys over who the best character was in the latest comic or television show. The kind of boy who was more likely to peak on the girl's shower than to successfully get a date with them. Allen was, by all rights, a nerd and so the First Change was both exciting and terrifying for him. For one, it gave him a new sense of confidence, but also places him in mortal danger nearly every moment of his life!<br /> <br /> When asked how someone with Allen's background could have been accepted into the tribe of some of the greatest Alphas in history, the young wolf answers with a smile. The first born did not ask Winter Wolf to pick up a spear and commence stabbing things, they asked him what their next course of action was. Any moron can learn to kill, but only a gifted few can keep those morons alive for any great length of time.<br /> <br /> This is how Allen earned himself the position of pack alpha, though he does occasionally clash with Hector who's more comfortable with the direct approach. Allen doesn't send his pack rushing into slaughter a problem, but rather he tries to outwit the problem, organizing his packmates into key positions before striking, and always having an escape route planned for if something goes wrong. Allen is a strategist and a mastermind, relying on his brains and his pack's brawn to win the day from the malicious spirits that plague the world. This has earned him the spirit name Trickster-of-Battle!<br /> <br /> <br /> --------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Hector (Crashes-the-Line) Macky</b><br /> <br /> <b>Concept:</b> Star Quarterback<br /> <b>Pack:</b> Teen Wolfpack<br /> <br /> <b>Auspice:</b> Rahu<br /> <b>Tribe:</b> Blood Talons<br /> <b>Age:</b> 17<br /> <br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Hope<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Pride<br /> <br /> <b>Primary Renown:</b> Purity, Glory, Honor<br /> <br /> <b>Gifts:</b> Strength, Dominance, Rage<br /> <b>Primal Urge:</b> 1<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 10/1<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Bio:</b> From a certain point of view, one might say that Hector has been training to be a warrior all his life. Although it was only high school, he was still one of the greatest foot ball players on the team, and proudly boasts about that touch down he got with 3 players from the other team clinging to his body! Unfortunately the first change put this testosterone fueled jock on overdrive and now his thirst for battle is becoming increasingly more difficult to restrain.<br /> <br /> Hector's first change was more of a curse for Hector personally than other Rahu might think. Hector was an athlete and never put any stock into spirituality or saving the trees. Now that he's a werewolf and has all the obligations that entails, he fears for what that will mean for his football scholarship and the life he once knew. How can he expect to go pro, when all it takes is one bad prank in the locker room or on the field to set him off? Fortunately, the spirit world is always willing to supply him with an outlet for his worries and frustrations.<br /> <br /> When the Teen Wolfpack was founding, Hector challenged Allen for the title of alpha, disbelieving that he could have been a Storm Lord. This lead to Hector being humiliated in front of the entire pack when the seemingly helpless Allen outmaneuvered the brawny superstar, using his own power against him to win the fight. Since then, Hector's impatient demeanor has clashed with Allen's more prudent one several times, but he has not openly challenged him again, realizing the benefits to Allen's method.<br /> <br /> Crashes-the-Line is a very good spirit name for Hector, because that is pretty much his plan of attack. When confronted with enemy ranks, he charges head on into the fold, slamming his body against the front lines and shattering the enemy formations. While they're trying to regroup or flee from the angry werewolf in the center of their their battle lines, the rest of his pack are able to circle around the disorganized troops.<br /> <br /> <br /> -------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Haley (War-Dancer) Holms</b><br /> <br /> <b>Concept:</b> Feisty Party Girl<br /> <b>Pack:</b> Teen Wolfpack<br /> <br /> <b>Auspice:</b> Cahalith<br /> <b>Tribe:</b> Iron Masters<br /> <b>Age:</b> 16<br /> <br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Charity<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Lust<br /> <br /> <b>Primary Renown:</b> Glory, Cunning, Honor<br /> <br /> <b>Gifts:</b> Inspiration, Shaping, Evasion<br /> <b>Primal Urge:</b> 2<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 11/1<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Bio:</b> Before the first change, Haley was a wild and untamed party girl. Now... well she's still the same thing, only to a much higher degree! Haley is overflowing with energy, and attends rave parties where hundreds of people in fluorescent accessories grind and dance the night away in a dimly lit room. What most people don't realize is that the booming music and gyrating bodies is actually her form of training, and is the reason she earned the name War-Dancer.<br /> <br /> Haley just recently hit her 16th birthday and is determined to enjoy the new freedoms that comes with that, one of which being the freedom to drive! Unfortunately her Sweet 16 party came in the form of her first change, and a barrage of wild hallucinations. Still a hell of a party, though, and she hopes for many more in the future.<br /> <br /> When Haley enters the field of battle, it is in a flashing of claws, fangs, and the occasional weapon depending on what form she's in. At the heights of her ecstatic fighting style, her attacks flow seamlessly between each other, like she's moving to her own rhythmic battle hymn. She's not as blood thirsty as Hector, but her high speed fighting style is no less violent.<br /> <br /> Haley is the life of the pack, for she enjoys life the most. When a hunt goes afoul, she usually knows the best ways to recover her packmate's self esteem. She enjoys loud music, dancing, underage drinking, recreational drugs (ecstasy and weed), and promiscuous sex. The last two being the riskiest, given her new existence. Few things are as wild as a Cahalith simultaneously receiving visions from Luna while tripping on ecstasy and surrounded by horny teenagers in a crowded rave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-04-2014, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-03T07:51:52-07:00","id":271621,"title":"","content":"<b>NOTE: </b>I did not know where to put Rituals as it doesn't really specify if they're a Merit, or if they go in the Gift section.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Rebecca (Witch-of-the-Wylds) Kline</b><br /> <br /> <b>Concept:</b> Angsty Gothic Pagan<br /> <b>Pack: </b>Teen Wolfpack<br /> <br /> <b>Auspice:</b> Ithaeur<br /> <b>Tribe:</b> Hunters in Darkness<br /> <b>Age:</b> 17<br /> <br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Justice<br /> <b>Vice: </b>Wrath<br /> <br /> <b>Primary Renown:</b> Wisdom, Purity, Glory<br /> <br /> <b>Gifts:</b> Elemental, Nature, Rituals 1<br /> <b>Primal Urge:</b> 3<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 12/1<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Bio:</b> Prior to the first change, Rebecca was undergoing the gothic phase in her life. A shut in from even her own family, dressing in black and performing fake rituals in her room as a way to get revenge on the preppy girls and guys at school. So when she finally did undergo the first change and awoke to the role of a shaman, it wasn't that big of a surprise. Now that her rituals and talismans are real, Rebecca is more dangerous than she has ever been. For the next time she places a hex on you, it's going to come true!<br /> <br /> Rebecca's first change has done nothing for growing her out of the gothic phase. In fact, it seems to have exasperated it! Most Goths come to realize they're acting foolish, and that their witchcraft is just pretend, and grow out of the scene. But for Rebecca, the magic is real, the spirits are real, and everyone else is acting foolish for ignoring their presence!<br /> <br /> When it comes to the rest of her pack, Rebecca is quite scary when she wants to be, and downright horrifying to their enemies. Her spirit name Witch-of-the-Wylds is very appropriate, for she wields her Gifts and Rituals with a passion unseen in the rest of her pack. She still believes in using her magic (for &quot;magic&quot; is the term she is most comfortable using) to invoke punishment upon those she feels deserves it, although her focus has shifted to be less on high school students, and on more serious threats plaguing the hunting grounds.<br /> <br /> The only one in the pack who seems unphased by the resident shaman is Kevin, who she prefers to hang out with. It is uncertain at this time whether they are simply friends or if there is any romantic interest going on, however.<br /> <br /> --------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>Kevin (Water-Tester) Maximus</b><br /> <br /> <b>Concept:</b> Eavesdropping Explorer<br /> <b>Pack:</b> Teen Wolfpack<br /> <br /> <b>Auspice:</b> Irraka<br /> <b>Tribe:</b> Bone Shadows<br /> <b>Age:</b> 18<br /> <br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Temperance<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Jealousy<br /> <br /> <b>Primary Renown:</b> Cunning, Wisdom, Purity<br /> <br /> <b>Gifts:</b> Stealth, New Moon, Rituals 1<br /> <b>Primal Urge:</b> 2<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 11/1<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Bio:</b> Not much can be said about Kevin prior to the first change aside from the fact he was overly curious. Having a compulsive need to eavesdrop on other conversations, or sneak his way into restricted access locations. He chose to remain in the background when possible, so even his own pack didn't know him before the first change awoke him to role of being the team scout.<br /> <br /> Kevin's spirit name Water-Tester may sound unusual and perhaps even insulting. But Kevin points out the meaning behind it. He is the scout, the explorer, the reconnaissance member of the pack. His role is to travel ahead of his packmates and check for traps, enemy defenses, and any weaknesses that may be exploited. He is the wolf who dips his toes into the pool to see if it is too hot or too cold before jumping in, he is the Water-Tester!<br /> <br /> Kevin is more of the quiet one of the group, possibly a left over trait from when he was human. He prefers to listen rather than speak, and being a fellow outsider, he gets along the most easily with Rebecca. Whether they are simply best friends, or if there is any romantic connection is up to the future to decide. Being a member of the Bone Shadows, he has some understanding of the various ceremonies that Rebecca invokes, while Haley, Allen, and Hector simply can't fathom their significance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T08:19:35-07:00","id":272221,"title":"","content":"All werewolves are demons. Jake Asby, or the &quot;Reverend&quot;, as his packmates call him, has known this to be a fact ever since his First Change. There is nothing that is natural about monsters that feel the Rage, that take the shape of 3 meters of wolf-death, that feel the need to hunt and to consume.<br /> <br /> If you ask Jake, he'll tell you that Hell isn't some sort of nebulous concept of an afterlife; it's here, now. And the Forsaken are its wardens and foremost devils.<br /> <br /> This is what Jake and his pack do, then: they punish sinners. As werewolves (demons), they cannot help their nature, but they can still channel it in productive ways - to hunt and punish those who sin against God's plan. The Hosts. The Pure. The Spirit-Ridden. Everyone who is a worse abomination in God's eyes than the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> For it is God's will.<br /> <br /> Jake Asby is a Storm Lord Cahalith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T09:18:58-07:00","id":272281,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I like it, leaves more room for character customization. Though he sounds more like a Ghost Wolf than somebody who would swear the oath of the moon.<br /> <br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> As a child, Curtis Myers arrived from school one day to find his family ripped to shreds by the Predator Kings. The shock and stress forced him to undergo the first change, and set him on an obsessive quest to find the pack responsible. He has earned himself the name Cold-Inferno in honor of the blazing hatred that continues to burn within him to this day. After being inducted into werewolf society, Curtis threw himself into studying the spirit world, in hopes of acquiring as much power and weapons as he can for the day he succeeds in finding his family's killers.<br /> <br /> Curtis Myers is a Bone Shadow Rahu<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> -----------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> Milly Adkins, otherwise known as Wailing-Death has a reputation for losing herself in the throws of battle. The only time she feels she is free is when she's ripping apart swathes of enemies with reckless abandon, shrieking and howling incoherently. During these outrages, it is unclear whether Milly is totally fearless, or possibly suicidal. When asked the reason for her sorrow, she merely replies that it is too complicated to put into words for those who don't experience it themselves.<br /> <br /> Milly Adkins is a Rahu that was converted to the Fire Touched shortly after her First Change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T11:32:17-07:00","id":272417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/271581-forsaken-character-suggestions?p=272281#post272281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, I like it, leaves more room for character customization. Though he sounds more like a Ghost Wolf than somebody who would swear the oath of the moon.</div> </div> </div> </div>The oath is Jake's Holy Code Of Behavior. He *despises* Ghost Wolves and other werewolves who refuse to be the best devils they can be. They're only very little better than the Pure in his eyes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T14:58:34-07:00","id":277580,"title":"","content":"Only starter PCs here? No sample Elders or anything of the sort?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3702-ursufgutha-storm-born","name":"Ursufgutha Storm-Born","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}